From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: a colour scheme switch keeps the desktop's colour

The visual style's colour schemes carry every system colour, the desktop's too, and switching scheme with the app
mode (light <-> dark, RefreshImmersiveColorPolicyState) wrote all of them: a solid desktop colour the person had
chosen went back to the scheme's at every switch. As on Windows, the switch now leaves COLOR_BACKGROUND alone.
---
diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
index bbd80a3..1e99142 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
@@ -617,6 +617,19 @@ static void UXTHEME_ApplyColorScheme(PTHEME_FILE tf)
     MSSTYLES_SetActiveTheme(tf, FALSE);
 
     count = MSSTYLES_GetThemeSysColors(tf, elements, colors, NUM_SYS_COLORS);
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SCHEME_SETS_DESKTOP
+    /* the desktop's colour is the person's (Settings > Personalization >
+     * Background), not the scheme's: switching to dark mode and back leaves
+     * it alone, as on Windows */
+    for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
+        if (elements[i] == COLOR_BACKGROUND)
+        {
+            memmove(elements + i, elements + i + 1, (count - i - 1) * sizeof(*elements));
+            memmove(colors + i, colors + i + 1, (count - i - 1) * sizeof(*colors));
+            count--;
+            i--;
+        }
+#endif
     if (count && !RegCreateKeyExW(HKEY_CURRENT_USER, strColorKey, 0, 0, 0, KEY_ALL_ACCESS, 0, &hKey, 0))
     {
         for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
